#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:0
msgid "Deploy dApps generated by QuickDapp to IPFS and link them to an ENS subdomain directly from Remix IDE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:0
msgid "deploy dapp, ipfs, ens, remixdapp.eth, quickdapp, remix ide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:8
msgid "Deploying a dApp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:11
msgid "This feature is only available to beta testers. Join the Remix beta program to get access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:14
msgid "You can deploy Dapps generated by {doc}`QuickDapp </quickdapp>` on IPFS and link them to an ENS domain directly from Remix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:16
msgid "Remix automatically provides a free ENS subdomain under `remixdapp.eth` for your Dapp with no gas fees required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:19
msgid "Deploying to IPFS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:21
msgid "Before you deploy to IPFS, you must have a smart contract compiled and deployed using the Deploy & Run plugin, and a Dapp generated by the QuickDapp plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:24
msgid "When you are configuring rules for the Dapp generation, ensure that you leave the \"**Create as Base Mini App**\" checkbox unchecked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:27
msgid "After QuickDapp generates your Dapp, expand the \"**Publish to IPFS**\" tab in QuickDapp's right panel and click the \"**Deploy to IPFS**\" button. This bundles and uploads your files to IPFS. Once the upload is complete, a `CID` (Content Identifier) is returned. This is a unique address that identifies your Dapp on the network and is used as the target when registering the ENS subdomain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:29
msgid "![The Publish to IPFS tab in the QuickDapp right panel, showing the Deploy to IPFS button and a generated CID after a successful upload](images/deploy_dapp/upload-ipfs.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:29
msgid "The Publish to IPFS tab in the QuickDapp right panel, showing the Deploy to IPFS button and a generated CID after a successful upload"
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:31
msgid "Register ENS Subdomain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:33
msgid "Once your Dapp is on IPFS, you can link it to a human-readable ENS subdomain under `remixdapp.eth` (e.g. `myapp.remixdapp.eth`) so users can access it without needing the raw CID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:35
msgid "Registration transactions are processed on **Arbitrum One (L2)**, with gas fees covered by the Remix backend, so you pay nothing. To register the subdomain, expand the \"**Register ENS (Arbitrum)**\" tab in the QuickDapp right panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:38
msgid "This tab only becomes visible after the deployment to IPFS is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:41
msgid "Enter your preferred subdomain name (e.g., `bridge.remixdapp.eth`) and Remix will check its availability. Once you have selected an available subdomain, click the \"**Register Subdomain**\" button and wait for the server to process the registration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:43
msgid "![The Register ENS (Arbitrum) tab in the QuickDapp right panel, showing the subdomain input field and Register Subdomain button](images/deploy_dapp/link-ens.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:43
msgid "The Register ENS (Arbitrum) tab in the QuickDapp right panel, showing the subdomain input field and Register Subdomain button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:46
msgid "The returned URLs have `.limo` appended (e.g. `myapp.remixdapp.eth.limo`). This is because standard web browsers cannot natively resolve `.eth` domains. `.limo` is a gateway service that resolves ENS names and serves the underlying IPFS content over HTTPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../deploy_dapp.md:50
msgid "Your Dapp is now live at https://[yourname].remixdapp.eth.limo."
msgstr ""
